1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:01,930
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:01,930 --> 00:00:04,110
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,110 --> 00:00:05,530
don't accept that.

4
00:00:05,530 --> 00:00:06,410
I had my right knee

5
00:00:06,410 --> 00:00:08,070
replaced two years ago.

6
00:00:08,070 --> 00:00:09,900
It has hurt every day
since.

7
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:11,410
Not surgery pain.

8
00:00:11,410 --> 00:00:12,890
I know what that felt
like,

9
00:00:12,890 --> 00:00:14,110
and it went away.

10
00:00:14,110 --> 00:00:15,350
This is different.

11
00:00:15,350 --> 00:00:16,340
Tight.

12
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:17,250
Full.

13
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:18,070
Like a band around

14
00:00:18,070 --> 00:00:20,070
the joint that never
loosens.

15
00:00:20,070 --> 00:00:21,010
And for two years

16
00:00:21,010 --> 00:00:22,640
I've been told the same
thing.

17
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:24,610
Give it time.

18
00:00:24,610 --> 00:00:26,410
At six weeks it was
swelling,

19
00:00:26,410 --> 00:00:27,740
and swelling is normal.

20
00:00:27,740 --> 00:00:28,550
At three months,

21
00:00:28,550 --> 00:00:29,790
give it six.

22
00:00:29,790 --> 00:00:31,050
At six months,

23
00:00:31,050 --> 00:00:33,640
some knees take a full
year.

24
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:34,580
At a year,

25
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:36,960
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

26
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:38,290
And I didn't just wait.

27
00:00:38,290 --> 00:00:39,880
We went down the list.

28
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:41,950
More physical therapy.

29
00:00:41,950 --> 00:00:42,950
Every session,

30
00:00:42,950 --> 00:00:44,900
every exercise at home.

31
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:46,230
I got stronger.

32
00:00:46,230 --> 00:00:47,970
The tightness never moved.

33
00:00:47,970 --> 00:00:49,410
The pain pills helped,

34
00:00:49,410 --> 00:00:51,360
and that was the problem.

35
00:00:51,360 --> 00:00:53,480
I'm already on enough
every morning,

36
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:54,430
and nobody could tell me

37
00:00:54,430 --> 00:00:55,650
when I'd get to stop.

38
00:00:55,650 --> 00:00:57,140
Then a nerve block.

39
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:58,960
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

40
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:00,490
And after that, a second

41
00:01:00,490 --> 00:01:01,570
operation to go back

42
00:01:01,570 --> 00:01:03,350
in and do it over.

43
00:01:03,350 --> 00:01:04,630
I said no.

44
00:01:04,630 --> 00:01:06,310
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

45
00:01:06,310 --> 00:01:07,230
and my knee felt like

46
00:01:07,230 --> 00:01:09,020
a band was wrapped around
it,

47
00:01:09,020 --> 00:01:11,870
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

48
00:01:11,870 --> 00:01:13,480
Every morning I took
something

49
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:14,530
for it and got

50
00:01:14,530 --> 00:01:15,790
on with my day.

51
00:01:15,790 --> 00:01:17,190
Couldn't do the stairs,

52
00:01:17,190 --> 00:01:18,360
couldn't stand at the
counter

53
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:19,850
long enough to finish
dinner,

54
00:01:19,850 --> 00:01:21,280
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

55
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:23,600
game without shifting
every two minutes.

56
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:25,540
It woke me at night,

57
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:27,500
and it turned ordinary
things,

58
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:28,610
like getting in the car

59
00:01:28,610 --> 00:01:30,010
or up off the couch,

60
00:01:30,010 --> 00:01:31,410
into a decision.

61
00:01:31,410 --> 00:01:32,620
After a long and serious

62
00:01:32,620 --> 00:01:33,860
talk with my husband,

63
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:35,620
I went back in one more
time.

64
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:36,730
That was the fourth set

65
00:01:36,730 --> 00:01:38,400
of X-rays on this knee.

66
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:40,750
And like the three before
it,

67
00:01:40,750 --> 00:01:43,510
the answer was everything
looks great.

68
00:01:43,510 --> 00:01:45,810
No loosening, no
infection,

69
00:01:45,810 --> 00:01:47,100
nothing wrong.

70
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:48,300
Only this time there

71
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:49,870
was no new number.

72
00:01:49,870 --> 00:01:50,660
Nobody said

73
00:01:50,660 --> 00:01:52,270
give it another six
months.

74
00:01:52,270 --> 00:01:54,100
There was nothing left to
give it.

75
00:01:54,100 --> 00:01:55,140
I sat in the parking

76
00:01:55,140 --> 00:01:56,330
lot for a while.

77
00:01:56,330 --> 00:01:57,890
Okay, I thought.

78
00:01:57,890 --> 00:01:59,490
Then explain this.

79
00:01:59,490 --> 00:02:01,380
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

80
00:02:01,380 --> 00:02:02,950
I hit my breaking point.

81
00:02:02,950 --> 00:02:04,990
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

82
00:02:04,990 --> 00:02:06,710
Everyone in the house was
asleep

83
00:02:06,710 --> 00:02:08,280
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

84
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:09,240
with my leg up,

85
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:10,800
trying to find any angle
where

86
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:11,980
it didn't feel like
something

87
00:02:11,980 --> 00:02:13,380
was wrapped around my knee

88
00:02:13,380 --> 00:02:14,990
and tightening.

89
00:02:14,990 --> 00:02:17,510
My husband didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

90
00:02:17,510 --> 00:02:19,740
By then I'd stopped
telling him.

91
00:02:19,740 --> 00:02:20,790
And I just thought,

92
00:02:20,790 --> 00:02:22,470
is this really my life
now?

93
00:02:22,470 --> 00:02:24,100
I can't live like this.

94
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:25,800
So I made myself a
promise.

95
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:26,600
I wouldn't go a day

96
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:28,290
without looking for an
answer.

97
00:02:28,290 --> 00:02:30,480
And when I found one,

98
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:31,570
I'd share it with everyone

99
00:02:31,570 --> 00:02:32,970
going through the same
thing.

100
00:02:32,970 --> 00:02:34,310
So I got my laptop

101
00:02:34,310 --> 00:02:36,050
out and went looking.

102
00:02:36,050 --> 00:02:37,350
Not for a product.

103
00:02:37,350 --> 00:02:38,720
For an explanation.

104
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:40,370
Mayo Clinic forums,

105
00:02:40,370 --> 00:02:42,820
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

106
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:45,770
doctor videos, medical
animations.

107
00:02:45,770 --> 00:02:46,780
And that's when I found

108
00:02:46,780 --> 00:02:48,440
a video from a physical
therapist

109
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:49,020
named Dr.

110
00:02:49,020 --> 00:02:51,170
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

111
00:02:51,170 --> 00:02:53,020
had been through exactly
this.

112
00:02:53,020 --> 00:02:54,470
But before I say anything
else,

113
00:02:54,470 --> 00:02:56,790
I want to be straight with
you.

114
00:02:56,790 --> 00:02:58,960
You've already had
something work fast.

115
00:02:58,960 --> 00:02:59,800
The ice.

116
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:01,260
The first week of a new
pill.

117
00:03:01,260 --> 00:03:02,890
The good day after a
session.

118
00:03:02,890 --> 00:03:03,950
Then it wore off.

119
00:03:03,950 --> 00:03:06,290
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

120
00:03:06,290 --> 00:03:08,040
Fast relief isn't relief.

121
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:09,370
It's a preview.

122
00:03:09,370 --> 00:03:10,490
So I'm not going to tell

123
00:03:10,490 --> 00:03:11,990
you this works fast.

124
00:03:11,990 --> 00:03:13,460
It doesn't.

125
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:15,350
But if you're willing to
be patient,

126
00:03:15,350 --> 00:03:16,280
and to look at what's

127
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:17,960
going on around your new
knee

128
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:19,690
instead of inside it,
there

129
00:03:19,690 --> 00:03:22,280
is a real reason it still
hurts.

130
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:24,690
And something you can do
about it.

131
00:03:24,690 --> 00:03:26,430
Let me explain what he
said,

132
00:03:26,430 --> 00:03:27,820
because this is what
changed

133
00:03:27,820 --> 00:03:29,470
everything for me.

134
00:03:29,470 --> 00:03:31,450
He started with the
basics.

135
00:03:31,450 --> 00:03:32,980
A knee replacement takes
out

136
00:03:32,980 --> 00:03:34,870
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

137
00:03:34,870 --> 00:03:36,500
in metal and plastic.

138
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:38,250
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

139
00:03:38,250 --> 00:03:40,000
you had before the
operation.

140
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,090
That part I already knew.

141
00:03:42,090 --> 00:03:43,530
But then he explained
something

142
00:03:43,530 --> 00:03:45,170
nobody had ever told me.

143
00:03:45,170 --> 00:03:46,310
He said,

144
00:03:46,310 --> 00:03:47,970
think about a swollen foot

145
00:03:47,970 --> 00:03:49,040
inside a shoe.

146
00:03:49,040 --> 00:03:50,450
The shoe didn't shrink.

147
00:03:50,450 --> 00:03:53,290
Your foot is taking up
more room,

148
00:03:53,290 --> 00:03:54,950
so everything feels
cramped

149
00:03:54,950 --> 00:03:57,010
and tight and squeezed.

150
00:03:57,010 --> 00:03:58,110
Your new knee sits

151
00:03:58,110 --> 00:03:59,580
in a limited space with
living

152
00:03:59,580 --> 00:04:01,630
tissue packed all around
it.

153
00:04:01,630 --> 00:04:03,500
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

154
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:05,330
had to work through that
tissue.

155
00:04:05,330 --> 00:04:08,210
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

156
00:04:08,210 --> 00:04:10,400
At first that's normal.

157
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:12,130
But in some people that
swelling can

158
00:04:12,130 --> 00:04:14,770
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

159
00:04:14,770 --> 00:04:16,540
And swollen tissue takes
up more

160
00:04:16,540 --> 00:04:18,510
room than calm tissue
does.

161
00:04:18,510 --> 00:04:20,530
So when you bend,

162
00:04:20,530 --> 00:04:23,050
that tissue gets
compressed.

163
00:04:23,050 --> 00:04:24,400
When you straighten,

164
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:25,970
it gets pulled tight.

165
00:04:25,970 --> 00:04:26,970
That's the band.

166
00:04:26,970 --> 00:04:29,190
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

167
00:04:29,190 --> 00:04:30,130
And you start being

168
00:04:30,130 --> 00:04:31,170
the one who says,

169
00:04:31,170 --> 00:04:32,520
you go ahead.

170
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:33,890
I'll stay here.

171
00:04:33,890 --> 00:04:35,520
And that's exactly why so
much

172
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:37,830
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

173
00:04:37,830 --> 00:04:39,770
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

174
00:04:39,770 --> 00:04:40,970
around the knee.

175
00:04:40,970 --> 00:04:41,860
Worth doing,

176
00:04:41,860 --> 00:04:43,180
and I'd done it.

177
00:04:43,180 --> 00:04:44,620
It does nothing about
tissue

178
00:04:44,620 --> 00:04:46,240
taking up room.

179
00:04:46,240 --> 00:04:47,620
A nerve block quiets

180
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:50,030
the nerve carrying the
signal.

181
00:04:50,030 --> 00:04:52,340
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

182
00:04:52,340 --> 00:04:53,850
But when that irritated
tissue

183
00:04:53,850 --> 00:04:55,350
finally calms down,

184
00:04:55,350 --> 00:04:56,740
it holds less fluid,

185
00:04:56,740 --> 00:04:58,480
and it takes up less room.

186
00:04:58,480 --> 00:05:00,050
Less room taken up means

187
00:05:00,050 --> 00:05:02,670
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

188
00:05:02,670 --> 00:05:04,730
That's what takes the
pressure off.

189
00:05:04,730 --> 00:05:05,780
After two years of this,

190
00:05:05,780 --> 00:05:08,150
it finally made sense.

191
00:05:08,150 --> 00:05:10,030
The problem was never the
new knee.

192
00:05:10,030 --> 00:05:12,520
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

193
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:14,370
He calls it the squeeze.

194
00:05:14,370 --> 00:05:17,030
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

195
00:05:17,030 --> 00:05:18,210
I'd bought knee sleeves,

196
00:05:18,210 --> 00:05:20,290
compression braces,
creams,

197
00:05:20,290 --> 00:05:21,730
half of Amazon really,

198
00:05:21,730 --> 00:05:23,170
and all any of it gave me

199
00:05:23,170 --> 00:05:24,230
was an hour.

200
00:05:24,230 --> 00:05:25,190
I even looked at going

201
00:05:25,190 --> 00:05:27,300
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

202
00:05:27,300 --> 00:05:28,900
But at $200 a session

203
00:05:28,900 --> 00:05:31,130
with nothing covered by
insurance,

204
00:05:31,130 --> 00:05:33,210
that was a quick no.

205
00:05:33,210 --> 00:05:34,580
Then one night I went

206
00:05:34,580 --> 00:05:35,970
back to that knee
replacement

207
00:05:35,970 --> 00:05:38,090
group and actually read
it.

208
00:05:38,090 --> 00:05:39,080
Thousands of people,

209
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:40,330
years out from surgery,

210
00:05:40,330 --> 00:05:42,670
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

211
00:05:42,670 --> 00:05:44,920
nobody could explain.

212
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:46,850
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

213
00:05:46,850 --> 00:05:48,900
the same thing kept coming
up.

214
00:05:48,900 --> 00:05:50,120
This one device,

215
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:51,450
and people saying it was
the first

216
00:05:51,450 --> 00:05:53,140
thing that made a
difference.

217
00:05:53,140 --> 00:05:55,110
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

218
00:05:55,110 --> 00:05:57,040
alright, here it comes,

219
00:05:57,040 --> 00:05:58,480
she's selling me something,

220
00:05:58,480 --> 00:06:00,170
let me shut that down
right now.

221
00:06:00,170 --> 00:06:01,770
I'm only here because I
made myself

222
00:06:01,770 --> 00:06:03,780
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

223
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:04,700
that if I ever found

224
00:06:04,700 --> 00:06:05,880
something that helped,

225
00:06:05,880 --> 00:06:07,770
I'd say so.

226
00:06:07,770 --> 00:06:10,290
It's called the KenRelief
Red

227
00:06:10,290 --> 00:06:12,800
Light Therapy Wrap.

228
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:14,950
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

229
00:06:14,950 --> 00:06:15,870
It looked like the cheap

230
00:06:15,870 --> 00:06:17,220
knee sleeves off Amazon

231
00:06:17,220 --> 00:06:18,960
that did nothing for me.

232
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:20,570
But I went to their
website anyway,

233
00:06:20,570 --> 00:06:21,340
just to see what all

234
00:06:21,340 --> 00:06:22,670
the fuss was about.

235
00:06:22,670 --> 00:06:24,250
It's the same red light
therapy

236
00:06:24,250 --> 00:06:26,520
clinics charge $200 a
session

237
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:28,710
for, off machines that
cost

238
00:06:28,710 --> 00:06:30,110
fifty thousand dollars,

239
00:06:30,110 --> 00:06:31,010
in a wrap you plug

240
00:06:31,010 --> 00:06:32,350
into the wall at home.

241
00:06:32,350 --> 00:06:33,990
Two hundred and forty
lights.

242
00:06:33,990 --> 00:06:36,110
Red at 660 nanometers

243
00:06:36,110 --> 00:06:38,500
and near-infrared at 850,

244
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:41,200
run together for the
strongest effect.

245
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:42,720
Four strength levels.

246
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:44,780
A five to thirty minute
timer.

247
00:06:44,780 --> 00:06:46,520
Then I saw the guarantee.

248
00:06:46,520 --> 00:06:47,830
Ninety days.

249
00:06:47,830 --> 00:06:49,840
Results or your money
back,

250
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:52,290
no questions, no store
credit,

251
00:06:52,290 --> 00:06:54,090
and you don't even send it
back.

252
00:06:54,090 --> 00:06:56,200
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

253
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:58,670
days to change my mind.

254
00:06:58,670 --> 00:06:59,830
There wasn't much to lose,

255
00:06:59,830 --> 00:07:00,870
so I ordered it.

256
00:07:00,870 --> 00:07:02,370
Two of them, actually.

257
00:07:02,370 --> 00:07:04,060
Only the right knee was
replaced,

258
00:07:04,060 --> 00:07:05,930
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

259
00:07:05,930 --> 00:07:07,830
and I'd done it for two
years.

260
00:07:07,830 --> 00:07:09,790
The left one was carrying
the difference.

261
00:07:09,790 --> 00:07:10,350
When it came,

262
00:07:10,350 --> 00:07:12,330
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

263
00:07:12,330 --> 00:07:13,430
because I'd been let down
too

264
00:07:13,430 --> 00:07:15,110
many times to get excited.

265
00:07:15,110 --> 00:07:17,380
What I felt was warmth.

266
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:19,230
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

267
00:07:19,230 --> 00:07:20,980
More like it was coming
from inside

268
00:07:20,980 --> 00:07:22,820
the knee and spreading
around it.

269
00:07:22,820 --> 00:07:24,090
And that was it.

270
00:07:24,090 --> 00:07:26,310
That was the whole
experience.

271
00:07:26,310 --> 00:07:27,470
When I took it off,

272
00:07:27,470 --> 00:07:28,350
I'll be honest,

273
00:07:28,350 --> 00:07:30,090
nothing dramatic had
happened.

274
00:07:30,090 --> 00:07:31,750
And after what that video
said,

275
00:07:31,750 --> 00:07:33,820
that's exactly what I
expected.

276
00:07:33,820 --> 00:07:34,840
What was different

277
00:07:34,840 --> 00:07:35,630
was that for the first

278
00:07:35,630 --> 00:07:36,890
time in two years

279
00:07:36,890 --> 00:07:38,480
I'd done something for my
knee

280
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:39,720
instead of to it.

281
00:07:39,720 --> 00:07:40,680
Twenty minutes,

282
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:41,960
